          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of a
            %em 2-category
            generalizes that of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category
            = succeed "." do
              %em hypercategories
          %p A 2-category consists of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"}> objects
                ;
            %li
              %p
                1-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                between objects;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
                between morphisms.
          %p
            The morphisms can be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composed
            along the objects, while the 2-morphisms can be composed in two different directions: along objects – called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"} horizontal composition
            – and along morphisms – called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+composition"} vertical composition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent"} coherent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
            2-morphisms.
          %p
            2-categories are also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+categorification"} horizontal categorification
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
          %p 2-categories provide the context for discussing
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"}> adjunction
                s;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"}> monad
                s.
          %p
            The concept of 2-category generalizes further in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-categories"} n-categories
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphism"} k-morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\le n
          %p
            2-categories form a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-category"} 3-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2Cat"} 2Cat
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#strict_2categories Strict 2-categories
          %p
            The easiest definition of 2-category is that it is a category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(x,y)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-category
          %h3#Weak General 2-categories
          %p
            For some purposes, strict 2-categories are too strict: one would like to allow composition of morphisms to be associative and unital only up to coherent invertible 2-morphisms. A direct generalization of the above “enriched” definition produces the classical notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
          %p
            One can also obtain notions of 2-category by specialization from the case of higher categories. Specifically, if we fix a meaning of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-category"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-category
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              \-category
            to be an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \geq 3
            = succeed "-morphisms," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "-categories," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            %em equal
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\geq 3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            of 2-morphisms instead of equivalence. (This is the case for both strict
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %p
            All of the above definitions produce “equivalent” theories of 2-category, although in some cases (such as the fact that every bicategory is equivalent to a strict 2-category) this requires some work to prove. On the nLab, we often use the word “2-category” in the general sense of referring to whatever model one may prefer, but usually one in which composition is weak; a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            is an adequate definition. One should beware, however, that in the literature it is common for “2-category” to refer only to
            %em strict
            2-categories.
          %p
            A 2-category in which all 1-morphisms and 2-morphisms are invertible is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The archetypical 2-category is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    objects are
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
                %li
                  %p
                    morphisms are
                    = succeed "s;" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                %li
                  %p
                    2-morphisms are
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                  %p
                    horizontal composition of 2-morphisms is the
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Godement+product"} Godement product
              %p
                This happens to be a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-category
            %li
              %p
                More generally, for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                any enriching category (such as a Benabou
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmos"} cosmos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V Cat
                whose
              %ul
                %li
                  objects are
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
                %li
                  morphisms are
                  = succeed "-enriched" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %li
                  2-morphisms are
                  = succeed "-natural" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %li
              %p
                On the other hand, for any such
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                we also have a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Prof"} Prof
                whose
              %ul
                %li
                  objects are
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
                %li
                  morphisms are
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  = succeed "s;" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
                %li 2-morphisms are natural transformations between these.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a category with
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Span"} Span
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C)
                whose
              %ul
                %li
                  objects are the objects of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %li
                  morphisms are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spans"} spans
                  in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %li 2-morphisms are morphisms of spans.
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                may be thought of as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}C
                (its
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    a single object
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bullet
                %li
                  %p
                    morphisms are the objects of
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi C
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi C
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mn 1
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 0
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}C)_1 = C_0
                %li
                  %p
                    2-morphisms are the morphisms of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                    \:
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi C
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mn 2
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}C)_2 = C_1
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"} horizontal composition
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}C
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+composition"} vertical composition
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}C
                is composition in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %p
                Conversely, every 2-category with a single object comes from a monoidal category this way, so the concepts are effectively equivalent. (Precisely: the 2-category of
                %em pointed
                2-categories with a single object is equivalent to that of monoidal categories). For more on this relation see
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+hypothesis"} delooping hypothesis
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+monoidal+n-category"} k-tuply monoidal n-category
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periodic+table"} periodic table
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
                is a 2-category. For instance
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    for
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                    any
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^2 A
                    is the strict 2-category with a single object, a single 1-morphisms, set of 2-moprhisms being
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                    and both horizontal composition as well as
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+composition"} vertical composition
                    being the product in
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi A
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %li
                  %p
                    for
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                    any
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                    is a 2-groupoid with a single object.
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                has a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+2-groupoid"} path 2-groupoid
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-category"} (∞,2)-category
                has a
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong homotopy 2-category
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#double_nerve Double nerve
          %p
            An ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            which is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+nerve"} double nerve
            which is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+set"} bisimplicial set
          %p
            There is also a 2-nerve. (
            %a{:href => "#LackPaoli"}> LackPaoli
            )
          %p (…)
          %h3#ModelCategoryStructure Model category structure
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on 2-categories – sometimes known as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folk+model+structure"} folk model structure
            – that models the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2Cat"} 2Cat
            (
            %a{:href => "#LackFolkModel"}> Lack
            ).
          %p
            For strict 2-categories this is the restriction of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folk+model+structure"} folk model structure
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+omega-categories"} strict omega-categories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The weak equivalences are the
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
            %li
              %p
                The acyclic fibrations are the
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-surjective+functor"} k-surjective functor
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %h4#FreeResolution Free resolutions
          %p
            %strong Theorem
            A strict 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is cofibrant precisely if the underlying 1-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"} free category
          %p
            This is theorem 4.8 in (
            %a{:href => "#LackStrict"}> LackStrict
            ). This is a special case of the more general statement that free strict
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computad"} computad
          %p
            %strong Example (free resolution of a 1-category).
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be an ordinary category (a 1-category) regarded as a strict 2-category. Then the cofibrant resolution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat C \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} C
            is the strict 2-category given as follows:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the objects of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat C
                are those of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                the morphisms of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat C
                are finite sequences of composable morphisms of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %p
                (hence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\hat C)_1
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"} free category
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quiver
                underlying
                = succeed ");" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                the 2-morphisms of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat C
                are
                %em generated
                from 2-morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
